  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: REAL TODAY, TEXT PARTLY STALE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096. Reproduces: `class A: class B: def go` gives class `B` (qualified_name `B`) and method `B.go` (qualified_name `B.go`); a doubly nested class is `C`. `A.B().go()` from a method and from a top-level function resolves to external_symbol `go` and `B` only. New fact: class-attribute fields already carry the full chain (`B.x` has qualified_name `A.B.x`, py.py:3620-3642), so one nested class emits two conventions. Two `B.go` methods under different outer classes share name and qualified_name and differ in stable_id. The py.py comment is now at 3551-3556 with different wording. `caller_symbol.name.split(\".\")[0]` is at py.py:7522 and 7560 (WI-fazid, open). Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/WI-naviz.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # b515
