  message: "[INVESTIGATION 2026-11-15, owner-requested, dev 03068d3531; report ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/naviz_agda_investigation_11152026/README.md] RECORD: ADR-0032 defines qualified_name as the fully-qualified scoped identifier; linkers/inheritance.py (_qualified_fits) already describes Python's value as the in-module qualname (OrderSerializer.Meta), which Python does not emit for a nested class; ten other analyzers emit the full type chain (Java, C#, Swift, Ruby, Rust, Scala, C++, TypeScript, Go, PHP); none emits a path-derived module name. PROTOTYPE (two lines in py.py: the field takes the chain the stable id already hashes; name and hash inputs untouched), measured against the same tree: fixture 6 names change; hypergumbo's own source 199 of 63,849 Python nodes; pretix 367 of 24,597. STABLE IDS MOVED: 0 in all three, so no scheme bump. EDGES: containment edges of nested classes go from the span fallback (0.9) to the name match (0.95): 3, 2 and 290; on pretix one extends edge is corrected: class Meta(OrderPositionSerializer.Meta) at api/serializers/order.py:644 pointed at WebHook.Meta in api/models.py:122 and now points at OrderPositionSerializer.Meta at order.py:595. No edge lost; pretix routes and usage contexts identical. NOT FIXED BY IT: A.B().go() still resolves to external_symbol stand-ins; that is the call resolver, filed separately today. WI-fazid's name.split is not reached (name unchanged). RECOMMENDATION TO THE OWNER: yes to the chain; no to the module path (inferred from layout, carried by the module-key axis and the file anchor already); correct the three ADR-0032 examples that show a module path. NOT MEASURED: a third corpus; verify-claims and taint. No status change."  # 6046
